From: OpenCode Android Full contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Keep all guest tasks attached to the supervisor lifetime

PRoot's --kill-on-exit handler cannot run when Android or the host sends
SIGKILL. Interactive shells and their foreground jobs may use different
process groups, so killing only the tracer's group can leave tasks behind.
Android 10+ kernels support PTRACE_O_EXITKILL (Linux 3.8+). Set it for every
initial tracee; the kernel inherits this option for traced fork/clone tasks.

--- a/src/tracee/event.c
+++ b/src/tracee/event.c
@@ -53,6 +53,10 @@
 #include "attribute.h"
 #include "compat.h"
 
+#ifndef PTRACE_O_EXITKILL
+#define PTRACE_O_EXITKILL 0x00100000
+#endif
+
 static bool seccomp_after_ptrace_enter = false;
 static bool seccomp_ptrace_event_supported = false;
 
@@ -547,7 +551,8 @@
 				PTRACE_O_TRACEVFORKDONE	|
 				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXEC	|
 				PTRACE_O_TRACECLONE	|
-				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXIT);
+				PTRACE_O_TRACEEXIT	|
+				PTRACE_O_EXITKILL);
 
 			/* Distinguish some events from others and
 			 * automatically trace each new process with
